# Better ADO Provider

`betterado` is a fork of the official
[`microsoft/azuredevops`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/microsoft/azuredevops)
provider. It inherits the full upstream resource set and adds resources Microsoft
has not implemented — most notably **classic release pipelines**
(`betterado_release_definition`) and **task groups** (`betterado_task_group`),
backed by the Azure DevOps Release Management REST API (`vsrm.dev.azure.com`, API
version 7.1).

Use the navigation to the left to read about the available resources.

## Example Usage

```terraform
terraform {
  required_providers {
    betterado = {
      source  = "parsoFish/betterado"
      version = "~> 0.1.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "betterado" {
  org_service_url       = "https://dev.azure.com/my-organization"
  personal_access_token = var.ado_pat
}

resource "betterado_release_definition" "app" {
  name       = "app-release"
  project_id = var.project_id

  environment {
    name = "Production"
    rank = 1

    deploy_phase {
      name       = "Agent job"
      rank       = 1
      phase_type = "agentBasedDeployment"
    }
  }
}
```

## Authentication

Authentication is performed with a
[Personal Access Token](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/organizations/accounts/use-personal-access-tokens-to-authenticate)
(PAT). The token can be supplied inline via `personal_access_token` or sourced
from the `AZDO_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` environment variable. The inherited
service-principal / OIDC / managed-identity methods from the upstream provider
are also available.

## Argument Reference

The following arguments are supported in the `provider` block:

- `org_service_url` - (Required) The Azure DevOps organization URL. May also be
  sourced from the `AZDO_ORG_SERVICE_URL` environment variable.
- `personal_access_token` - The Azure DevOps personal access token. May also be
  sourced from the `AZDO_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` environment variable.

Service-principal and OIDC arguments (`client_id`, `tenant_id`, `client_secret`,
`use_oidc`, `use_msi`, `use_cli`, and related `*_file_path` variants) are
inherited unchanged from the upstream provider.

